  "body": "https://compat.spec.whatwg.org/commit-snapshots/3ca5920dc59b351756399bab9ded097d963a799f/#ua-string-pattern-firefox\r\n\r\nAt the very least there seems to be a missing `;` after `<oscpu>`. If we only made that change then we'd say something like:\r\n\r\n- Desktop: `<platform>` = `Windows NT 10.0`, `<oscpu>` = `Win64; x64`\r\n- Mobile: `<platform>` = `Android 10`, `<oscpu>` = `Mobile`.\r\n\r\nBut this doesn't seem right. `Mobile` seems more like it'd be a `<deviceCompat>` token. And `<oscpu>` having semicolons inside of it is a bit... unusual. Maybe fine though.",
